        "carbs_g": 69
      },
      "prep_time": "15 minutes",
      "cook_time": "25 minutes",
      "ingredients": [
        "7.5 oz chicken breast per serving (2 lbs total for family of 4)",
        "1.5 cups cooked white rice per serving (3 cups dry for family)",
        "2 ears fresh corn, kernels cut off",
        "2 medium zucchini, diced small",
        "1 tbsp olive oil (total, family)",
        "4 tbsp plain Greek yogurt (for corn sauce, 1 tbsp per serving)",
        "2 tbsp cotija cheese crumbled (0.5 tbsp per serving)",
        "1 tbsp lime juice",
        "Fresh cilantro optional for adults"
      ],
      "steps": [
        "Cook white rice according to package directions to yield 6 cups cooked total.",
        "Season chicken breasts lightly with garlic powder, onion powder, and salt.",
        "Heat a large skillet or grill pan over medium heat. Use 1 tbsp olive oil across the whole pan.",
        "Cook chicken breasts 6-7 minutes per side until internal temperature reaches 165°F. Remove and rest 5 minutes, then slice.",
        "In the same pan over medium heat, add corn kernels and diced zucchini. Cook 5-6 minutes until tender and lightly golden, stirring frequently.",
        "Mix Greek yogurt with lime juice and a pinch of salt to make a mild corn sauce.",
        "Plate 1.5 cups rice per serving, top with corn and zucchini mixture, place sliced chicken alongside, drizzle with yogurt sauce, and sprinkle cotija cheese."
